{
  "_edit": "SOURCE — you own this file. Edit freely, by hand or by agent.",
  "_comment": [
    "HAND-AUTHORED. The rules that decide which job postings are worth an application.",
    "Read by scripts/score-job.js (`npm run score -- <slug|file>`) and by the email watch",
    "that screens job-alert mail. Nothing here is a fact about the candidate: it is a",
    "preference, so it never feeds the CV, the letter or the website.",
    "",
    "Scoring: each group adds up to `weight` points. A group earns weight * min(1, hits/saturate),",
    "where `hits` is the number of DISTINCT terms found in the posting. `penalties` subtract",
    "their points once if any term matches. Any `dealbreakers` term sets the verdict to `skip`,",
    "whatever the score. The total is clamped to 0..100.",
    "",
    "Terms are matched case-insensitively on word boundaries. A term that starts with `re:` is a",
    "JavaScript regular expression instead.",
    "",
    "This repo is PUBLIC. Keep pay floors, current-employer details and anything else private OUT",
    "of this file. The watch keeps those in the owner's private notes, not here.",
    "",
    "STATUS: second proposal (2026-11-13). Widened after the owner said any role that fits the skill set counts, finance and quant included. Not confirmed yet."
  ],
